{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every adapter implements the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":" contract, so they're interchangeable\nin "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":". This page is the full option reference: each adapter's options with\nan example of each."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#common-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common options"}]},{"type":"text","value":", shared by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inMemory()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redis()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapters: "},{"type":"link","href":"#inmemory","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inMemory()"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"#redis","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redis()"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"#hindsight","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hindsight()"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"#mem0","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mem0()"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"#honcho","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"honcho()"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#third-party-adapters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Third-party adapters"}]},{"type":"text","value":", published outside TanStack AI"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inMemory()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redis()"},{"type":"text","value":" are both client-side rankers built on the same pipeline, so\nthey share these options."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"topK"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"6"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Max hits returned by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"minScore"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.15"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Drop hits scoring below this."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"kinds"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Array<MemoryKind>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"all"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Restrict recall to these record kinds ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'message'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'summary'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'fact'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'preference'"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"embedder"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ embed(text): Promise<number[]> }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enable semantic scoring (embeds on both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"extract"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(turn, scope) => ExtractedFact[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persist derived facts on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":", alongside the raw turn."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"render"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(hits) => string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"built-in"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace the prompt renderer."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every option, in one adapter:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\n\n// `embedText` stands in for your embedding client (OpenAI, Cohere, a local model).\ndeclare function embedText(text: string): Promise<Array<number>>\n\nconst memory = inMemory({\n  topK: 8, // return up to 8 hits\n  minScore: 0.2, // ignore weak matches\n  kinds: ['message', 'fact', 'preference'], // skip summaries\n  embedder: { embed: embedText }, // semantic + lexical scoring\n  extract: (turn) => [\n    // store a derived fact in addition to the raw turn\n    { text: `User said: ${turn.user}`, kind: 'fact', importance: 0.8 },\n  ],\n  render: (hits) =>\n    // custom prompt block instead of the default renderer\n    `What I remember:\\n${hits.map((h) => `- ${h.record.text}`).join('\\n')}`,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"extract"}]},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ExtractedFact[]"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ text, kind?, importance?, metadata? }"},{"type":"text","value":"). Return\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" for a no-op. It's where an LLM-based fact extractor plugs in without the\nadapter taking a hard dependency on any model."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"embedder"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is invoked on the recall path (to embed the query) and again on save (to\nembed stored text). Without it, scoring is lexical + recency only."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"inmemory","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inMemory()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Zero-dependency, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Map"},{"type":"text","value":"-backed. Takes only the "},{"type":"link","href":"#common-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"common options"}]},{"type":"text","value":" above.\nRecords vanish on restart, so use it for dev, tests, and single-process demos."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\n\nconst memory = inMemory() // all options are optional","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"redis","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redis()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Plain-Redis adapter. Adds two options to the "},{"type":"link","href":"#common-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"common options"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and\nrequires a client."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redis"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RedisLike"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(required)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your Redis client ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ioredis"},{"type":"text","value":", or node-redis via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fromNodeRedis"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prefix"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'tanstack-ai:memory'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Key namespace."}]}]]},{"type":"code","value":"import Redis from 'ioredis'\nimport { redis } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/redis'\n\nconst memory = redis({\n  redis: new Redis(process.env.REDIS_URL ?? 'redis://localhost:6379'), // required\n  prefix: 'myapp:memory', // key namespace\n  topK: 8, // common options apply here too\n  minScore: 0.2,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"node-redis"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redis"},{"type":"text","value":" package) instead of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ioredis"},{"type":"text","value":"? Its camelCase API doesn't\nmatch "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RedisLike"},{"type":"text","value":", so wrap it with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fromNodeRedis"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createClient } from 'redis'\nimport { redis, fromNodeRedis } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/redis'\n\nconst client = createClient({ url: process.env.REDIS_URL })\nawait client.connect()\n\nconst memory = redis({ redis: fromNodeRedis(client) })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ioredis"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redis"},{"type":"text","value":" are both optional peer dependencies. Install whichever you use."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scope fields:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" index keys are "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{prefix}:index:{tenantId|_}:{userId|_}:{threadId}"},{"type":"text","value":"\n(each segment escaped so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":":"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\\"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"_"},{"type":"text","value":" in values cannot collide). Missing optional\ndims become "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"_"},{"type":"text","value":", so a write with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tenantId"},{"type":"text","value":" and a read without it hit "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"different"}]},{"type":"text","value":" keys\n— always pass the same dims you wrote with. There is no dual-read of older layouts; if\nyou previously wrote under a different index shape, reindex or wipe."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"which-scope-fields-each-adapter-honors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Which "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Scope"},{"type":"text","value":" fields each adapter honors"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"userId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tenantId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"namespace"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inMemory()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes (exact)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes (exact)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes (exact)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ignored"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redis()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes (key segment)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes (key segment)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes (key segment)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ignored"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hindsight()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes (bank id)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes (bank id / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"user"},{"type":"text","value":" option)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes (bank prefix; unset → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"_"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ignored"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mem0()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run_id"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"user_id"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"user"},{"type":"text","value":" option)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"no"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ignored"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"honcho()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes (session key)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes (peer id / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"user"},{"type":"text","value":" option)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes (session/peer prefix)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ignored"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional dims are exact-match (omit ≠ match any). mem0 does not model tenants —\nencode multi-tenant isolation into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"user"},{"type":"text","value":" if needed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"hindsight","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hindsight()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hosted adapter backed by Hindsight. Owns extraction/ranking server-side and exposes\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"retain"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reflect"},{"type":"text","value":" LLM tools through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@vectorize-io/hindsight-client"},{"type":"text","value":"\nis an optional peer, loaded lazily."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"user"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scope.userId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Durable user id used in the bank key ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{tenant|_}__{user}__{threadId}"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseUrl"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HINDSIGHT_URL"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"http://localhost:8888"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server URL."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"budget"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'low' | 'mid' | 'high'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'mid'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recall budget."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onToolRetain"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(receipt) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fired when the model calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hindsight_retain"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onToolRecall"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(query, result) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fired when the model calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hindsight_recall"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"code","value":"import { hindsight } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/hindsight'\n\nconst memory = hindsight({\n  user: 'alice', // bank = {_}__alice__{threadId} (or tenant__alice__{threadId})\n  baseUrl: 'https://hindsight.internal', // default: HINDSIGHT_URL\n  budget: 'high', // deeper recall\n  onToolRetain: (receipt) => console.log('model retained', receipt.ok),\n  onToolRecall: (query, result) =>\n    console.log('model recalled', query, result.fragments?.length),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bank id is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{tenantId|_}__{user}__{threadId}"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"mem0","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mem0()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hosted adapter backed by a mem0 server, over plain HTTP (no SDK peer). Requires a running\nmem0 server."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"user"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scope.userId"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'demo-user'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"mem0 "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"user_id"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseUrl"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MEM0_URL"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"http://localhost:8000"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server URL."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"apiKey"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MEM0_ADMIN_API_KEY"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bearer token."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rerank"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ask mem0 to rerank search results."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threshold"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Minimum search score."}]}]]},{"type":"code","value":"import { mem0 } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/mem0'\n\nconst memory = mem0({\n  user: 'alice', // mem0 user_id\n  baseUrl: 'https://mem0.internal', // default: MEM0_URL\n  apiKey: process.env.MEM0_ADMIN_API_KEY, // bearer token\n  rerank: true, // rerank results\n  threshold: 0.2, // stricter score floor\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"mem0 requests send "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"user_id"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run_id"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":"). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tenantId"},{"type":"text","value":" is not sent."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"honcho","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"honcho()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hosted adapter backed by Honcho. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":" returns a synthesized dialectic answer over the\nuser's representation (no discrete fragments). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@honcho-ai/sdk"},{"type":"text","value":" is an optional peer,\nloaded lazily."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"user"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scope.userId"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'demo-user'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"User peer id."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseURL"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HONCHO_URL"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"http://localhost:8001"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server URL."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"workspaceId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HONCHO_APP_NAME"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'ai-memory'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Workspace id."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"apiKey"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HONCHO_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'dev-no-auth'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API key."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"assistantId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'assistant'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Assistant peer id."}]}]]},{"type":"code","value":"import { honcho } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/honcho'\n\nconst memory = honcho({\n  user: 'alice', // user peer\n  baseURL: 'https://honcho.internal', // default: HONCHO_URL\n  workspaceId: 'my-app', // default: HONCHO_APP_NAME\n  apiKey: process.env.HONCHO_API_KEY, // default: 'dev-no-auth'\n  assistantId: 'support-bot', // default: 'assistant'\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Honcho session key is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{tenantId|_}__{threadId}"},{"type":"text","value":"; peers are "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{tenantId}__{user}"},{"type":"text","value":" when\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tenantId"},{"type":"text","value":" is set, otherwise the bare user id."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"third-party-adapters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Third-party adapters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These adapters are published and maintained outside TanStack AI. They implement the same\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":" contract, so they drop into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" like the ones above."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Backend"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recall"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../community-adapters/upstash#memory","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"upstashMemory()"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai/memory"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Upstash Redis (HTTP client)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"BM25 full-text query in Redis Search"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"upstashMemory()"},{"type":"text","value":" passes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runMemoryAdapterContract"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-memory/testkit"},{"type":"text","value":".\nUnlike "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redis()"},{"type":"text","value":", it ranks in Redis instead of loading records to rank client-side, and\nit honors "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"namespace"},{"type":"text","value":" as well as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tenantId"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"userId"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"where-to-go-next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where to go next"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":" contract and how a turn flows"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./quickstart","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quickstart"}]},{"type":"text","value":": wire an adapter into a real "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./operating","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Operating memory"}]},{"type":"text","value":": options, telemetry, devtools events, and failures"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./custom-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":": implement "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":" for a backend that isn't shipped"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"common-options","text":"Common options","level":2},{"id":"inmemory","text":"inMemory()","level":2},{"id":"redis","text":"redis()","level":2},{"id":"which-scope-fields-each-adapter-honors","text":"Which Scope fields each adapter honors","level":2},{"id":"hindsight","text":"hindsight()","level":2},{"id":"mem0","text":"mem0()","level":2},{"id":"honcho","text":"honcho()","level":2},{"id":"third-party-adapters","text":"Third-party adapters","level":2},{"id":"where-to-go-next","text":"Where to go next","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nEvery adapter implements the same `recall`/`save` contract, so they're interchangeable\nin `memoryMiddleware`. This page is the full option reference: each adapter's options with\nan example of each.\n\n- [Common options](#common-options), shared by `inMemory()` and `redis()`\n- Adapters: [`inMemory()`](#inmemory), [`redis()`](#redis), [`hindsight()`](#hindsight), [`mem0()`](#mem0), [`honcho()`](#honcho)\n- [Third-party adapters](#third-party-adapters), published outside TanStack AI\n\n## Common options\n\n`inMemory()` and `redis()` are both client-side rankers built on the same pipeline, so\nthey share these options.\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Purpose |\n|--------|------|---------|---------|\n| `topK` | `number` | `6` | Max hits returned by `recall`. |\n| `minScore` | `number` | `0.15` | Drop hits scoring below this. |\n| `kinds` | `Array<MemoryKind>` | all | Restrict recall to these record kinds (`'message'`, `'summary'`, `'fact'`, `'preference'`). |\n| `embedder` | `{ embed(text): Promise<number[]> }` | none | Enable semantic scoring (embeds on both `recall` and `save`). |\n| `extract` | `(turn, scope) => ExtractedFact[]` | none | Persist derived facts on `save`, alongside the raw turn. |\n| `render` | `(hits) => string` | built-in | Replace the prompt renderer. |\n\nEvery option, in one adapter:\n\n```ts\nimport { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\n\n// `embedText` stands in for your embedding client (OpenAI, Cohere, a local model).\ndeclare function embedText(text: string): Promise<Array<number>>\n\nconst memory = inMemory({\n  topK: 8, // return up to 8 hits\n  minScore: 0.2, // ignore weak matches\n  kinds: ['message', 'fact', 'preference'], // skip summaries\n  embedder: { embed: embedText }, // semantic + lexical scoring\n  extract: (turn) => [\n    // store a derived fact in addition to the raw turn\n    { text: `User said: ${turn.user}`, kind: 'fact', importance: 0.8 },\n  ],\n  render: (hits) =>\n    // custom prompt block instead of the default renderer\n    `What I remember:\\n${hits.map((h) => `- ${h.record.text}`).join('\\n')}`,\n})\n```\n\n**`extract`** returns `ExtractedFact[]` (`{ text, kind?, importance?, metadata? }`). Return\n`undefined` for a no-op. It's where an LLM-based fact extractor plugs in without the\nadapter taking a hard dependency on any model.\n\n**`embedder`** is invoked on the recall path (to embed the query) and again on save (to\nembed stored text). Without it, scoring is lexical + recency only.\n\n## `inMemory()`\n\nZero-dependency, `Map`-backed. Takes only the [common options](#common-options) above.\nRecords vanish on restart, so use it for dev, tests, and single-process demos.\n\n```ts\nimport { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\n\nconst memory = inMemory() // all options are optional\n```\n\n## `redis()`\n\nPlain-Redis adapter. Adds two options to the [common options](#common-options), and\nrequires a client.\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Purpose |\n|--------|------|---------|---------|\n| `redis` | `RedisLike` | (required) | Your Redis client (`ioredis`, or node-redis via `fromNodeRedis`). |\n| `prefix` | `string` | `'tanstack-ai:memory'` | Key namespace. |\n\n```ts\nimport Redis from 'ioredis'\nimport { redis } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/redis'\n\nconst memory = redis({\n  redis: new Redis(process.env.REDIS_URL ?? 'redis://localhost:6379'), // required\n  prefix: 'myapp:memory', // key namespace\n  topK: 8, // common options apply here too\n  minScore: 0.2,\n})\n```\n\nUsing **node-redis** (`redis` package) instead of `ioredis`? Its camelCase API doesn't\nmatch `RedisLike`, so wrap it with `fromNodeRedis`:\n\n```ts\nimport { createClient } from 'redis'\nimport { redis, fromNodeRedis } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/redis'\n\nconst client = createClient({ url: process.env.REDIS_URL })\nawait client.connect()\n\nconst memory = redis({ redis: fromNodeRedis(client) })\n```\n\n`ioredis` and `redis` are both optional peer dependencies. Install whichever you use.\n\n**Scope fields:** index keys are `{prefix}:index:{tenantId|_}:{userId|_}:{threadId}`\n(each segment escaped so `:`, `\\`, and `_` in values cannot collide). Missing optional\ndims become `_`, so a write with `tenantId` and a read without it hit **different** keys\n— always pass the same dims you wrote with. There is no dual-read of older layouts; if\nyou previously wrote under a different index shape, reindex or wipe.\n\n## Which `Scope` fields each adapter honors\n\n| Adapter | `threadId` | `userId` | `tenantId` | `namespace` |\n|---------|------------|----------|------------|-------------|\n| `inMemory()` | yes (exact) | yes (exact) | yes (exact) | ignored |\n| `redis()` | yes (key segment) | yes (key segment) | yes (key segment) | ignored |\n| `hindsight()` | yes (bank id) | yes (bank id / `user` option) | yes (bank prefix; unset → `_`) | ignored |\n| `mem0()` | yes (`run_id`) | yes (`user_id` / `user` option) | **no** | ignored |\n| `honcho()` | yes (session key) | yes (peer id / `user` option) | yes (session/peer prefix) | ignored |\n\nOptional dims are exact-match (omit ≠ match any). mem0 does not model tenants —\nencode multi-tenant isolation into `user` if needed.\n\n## `hindsight()`\n\nHosted adapter backed by Hindsight. Owns extraction/ranking server-side and exposes\n`retain`/`recall`/`reflect` LLM tools through `recall`. `@vectorize-io/hindsight-client`\nis an optional peer, loaded lazily.\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Purpose |\n|--------|------|---------|---------|\n| `user` | `string` | `scope.userId` | Durable user id used in the bank key (`{tenant\\|_}__{user}__{threadId}`). |\n| `baseUrl` | `string` | `HINDSIGHT_URL` / `http://localhost:8888` | Server URL. |\n| `budget` | `'low' \\| 'mid' \\| 'high'` | `'mid'` | Recall budget. |\n| `onToolRetain` | `(receipt) => void` | none | Fired when the model calls `hindsight_retain`. |\n| `onToolRecall` | `(query, result) => void` | none | Fired when the model calls `hindsight_recall`. |\n\n```ts\nimport { hindsight } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/hindsight'\n\nconst memory = hindsight({\n  user: 'alice', // bank = {_}__alice__{threadId} (or tenant__alice__{threadId})\n  baseUrl: 'https://hindsight.internal', // default: HINDSIGHT_URL\n  budget: 'high', // deeper recall\n  onToolRetain: (receipt) => console.log('model retained', receipt.ok),\n  onToolRecall: (query, result) =>\n    console.log('model recalled', query, result.fragments?.length),\n})\n```\n\nBank id is `{tenantId|_}__{user}__{threadId}`.\n\n## `mem0()`\n\nHosted adapter backed by a mem0 server, over plain HTTP (no SDK peer). Requires a running\nmem0 server.\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Purpose |\n|--------|------|---------|---------|\n| `user` | `string` | `scope.userId` / `'demo-user'` | mem0 `user_id`. |\n| `baseUrl` | `string` | `MEM0_URL` / `http://localhost:8000` | Server URL. |\n| `apiKey` | `string` | `MEM0_ADMIN_API_KEY` | Bearer token. |\n| `rerank` | `boolean` | `true` | Ask mem0 to rerank search results. |\n| `threshold` | `number` | `0.1` | Minimum search score. |\n\n```ts\nimport { mem0 } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/mem0'\n\nconst memory = mem0({\n  user: 'alice', // mem0 user_id\n  baseUrl: 'https://mem0.internal', // default: MEM0_URL\n  apiKey: process.env.MEM0_ADMIN_API_KEY, // bearer token\n  rerank: true, // rerank results\n  threshold: 0.2, // stricter score floor\n})\n```\n\nmem0 requests send `user_id` and `run_id` (`threadId`). `tenantId` is not sent.\n\n## `honcho()`\n\nHosted adapter backed by Honcho. `recall` returns a synthesized dialectic answer over the\nuser's representation (no discrete fragments). `@honcho-ai/sdk` is an optional peer,\nloaded lazily.\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Purpose |\n|--------|------|---------|---------|\n| `user` | `string` | `scope.userId` / `'demo-user'` | User peer id. |\n| `baseURL` | `string` | `HONCHO_URL` / `http://localhost:8001` | Server URL. |\n| `workspaceId` | `string` | `HONCHO_APP_NAME` / `'ai-memory'` | Workspace id. |\n| `apiKey` | `string` | `HONCHO_API_KEY` / `'dev-no-auth'` | API key. |\n| `assistantId` | `string` | `'assistant'` | Assistant peer id. |\n\n```ts\nimport { honcho } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/honcho'\n\nconst memory = honcho({\n  user: 'alice', // user peer\n  baseURL: 'https://honcho.internal', // default: HONCHO_URL\n  workspaceId: 'my-app', // default: HONCHO_APP_NAME\n  apiKey: process.env.HONCHO_API_KEY, // default: 'dev-no-auth'\n  assistantId: 'support-bot', // default: 'assistant'\n})\n```\n\nHoncho session key is `{tenantId|_}__{threadId}`; peers are `{tenantId}__{user}` when\n`tenantId` is set, otherwise the bare user id.\n\n## Third-party adapters\n\nThese adapters are published and maintained outside TanStack AI. They implement the same\n`recall`/`save` contract, so they drop into `memoryMiddleware` like the ones above.\n\n| Adapter | Package | Backend | Recall |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [`upstashMemory()`](../community-adapters/upstash#memory) | `@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai/memory` | Upstash Redis (HTTP client) | BM25 full-text query in Redis Search |\n\n`upstashMemory()` passes `runMemoryAdapterContract` from `@tanstack/ai-memory/testkit`.\nUnlike `redis()`, it ranks in Redis instead of loading records to rank client-side, and\nit honors `namespace` as well as `tenantId`, `userId`, and `threadId`.\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- [Overview](./overview): the `recall`/`save` contract and how a turn flows\n- [Quickstart](./quickstart): wire an adapter into a real `chat()` call\n- [Operating memory](./operating): options, telemetry, devtools events, and failures\n- [Custom Adapter](./custom-adapter): implement `recall`/`save` for a backend that isn't shipped\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Adapters\nid: memory-adapters\norder: 3\ndescription: \"Every built-in and vendor memory adapter in @tanstack/ai-memory, with all of their options and an example of each: inMemory, redis, hindsight, mem0, honcho.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - memory\n  - adapters\n  - inMemory\n  - redis\n  - hindsight\n  - mem0\n  - honcho\n  - options\n---\n\nEvery adapter implements the same `recall`/`save` contract, so they're interchangeable\nin `memoryMiddleware`. This page is the full option reference: each adapter's options with\nan example of each.\n\n- [Common options](#common-options), shared by `inMemory()` and `redis()`\n- Adapters: [`inMemory()`](#inmemory), [`redis()`](#redis), [`hindsight()`](#hindsight), [`mem0()`](#mem0), [`honcho()`](#honcho)\n- [Third-party adapters](#third-party-adapters), published outside TanStack AI\n\n## Common options\n\n`inMemory()` and `redis()` are both client-side rankers built on the same pipeline, so\nthey share these options.\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Purpose |\n|--------|------|---------|---------|\n| `topK` | `number` | `6` | Max hits returned by `recall`. |\n| `minScore` | `number` | `0.15` | Drop hits scoring below this. |\n| `kinds` | `Array<MemoryKind>` | all | Restrict recall to these record kinds (`'message'`, `'summary'`, `'fact'`, `'preference'`). |\n| `embedder` | `{ embed(text): Promise<number[]> }` | none | Enable semantic scoring (embeds on both `recall` and `save`). |\n| `extract` | `(turn, scope) => ExtractedFact[]` | none | Persist derived facts on `save`, alongside the raw turn. |\n| `render` | `(hits) => string` | built-in | Replace the prompt renderer. |\n\nEvery option, in one adapter:\n\n```ts\nimport { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\n\n// `embedText` stands in for your embedding client (OpenAI, Cohere, a local model).\ndeclare function embedText(text: string): Promise<Array<number>>\n\nconst memory = inMemory({\n  topK: 8, // return up to 8 hits\n  minScore: 0.2, // ignore weak matches\n  kinds: ['message', 'fact', 'preference'], // skip summaries\n  embedder: { embed: embedText }, // semantic + lexical scoring\n  extract: (turn) => [\n    // store a derived fact in addition to the raw turn\n    { text: `User said: ${turn.user}`, kind: 'fact', importance: 0.8 },\n  ],\n  render: (hits) =>\n    // custom prompt block instead of the default renderer\n    `What I remember:\\n${hits.map((h) => `- ${h.record.text}`).join('\\n')}`,\n})\n```\n\n**`extract`** returns `ExtractedFact[]` (`{ text, kind?, importance?, metadata? }`). Return\n`undefined` for a no-op. It's where an LLM-based fact extractor plugs in without the\nadapter taking a hard dependency on any model.\n\n**`embedder`** is invoked on the recall path (to embed the query) and again on save (to\nembed stored text). Without it, scoring is lexical + recency only.\n\n## `inMemory()`\n\nZero-dependency, `Map`-backed. Takes only the [common options](#common-options) above.\nRecords vanish on restart, so use it for dev, tests, and single-process demos.\n\n```ts\nimport { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\n\nconst memory = inMemory() // all options are optional\n```\n\n## `redis()`\n\nPlain-Redis adapter. Adds two options to the [common options](#common-options), and\nrequires a client.\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Purpose |\n|--------|------|---------|---------|\n| `redis` | `RedisLike` | (required) | Your Redis client (`ioredis`, or node-redis via `fromNodeRedis`). |\n| `prefix` | `string` | `'tanstack-ai:memory'` | Key namespace. |\n\n```ts\nimport Redis from 'ioredis'\nimport { redis } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/redis'\n\nconst memory = redis({\n  redis: new Redis(process.env.REDIS_URL ?? 'redis://localhost:6379'), // required\n  prefix: 'myapp:memory', // key namespace\n  topK: 8, // common options apply here too\n  minScore: 0.2,\n})\n```\n\nUsing **node-redis** (`redis` package) instead of `ioredis`? Its camelCase API doesn't\nmatch `RedisLike`, so wrap it with `fromNodeRedis`:\n\n```ts\nimport { createClient } from 'redis'\nimport { redis, fromNodeRedis } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/redis'\n\nconst client = createClient({ url: process.env.REDIS_URL })\nawait client.connect()\n\nconst memory = redis({ redis: fromNodeRedis(client) })\n```\n\n`ioredis` and `redis` are both optional peer dependencies. Install whichever you use.\n\n**Scope fields:** index keys are `{prefix}:index:{tenantId|_}:{userId|_}:{threadId}`\n(each segment escaped so `:`, `\\`, and `_` in values cannot collide). Missing optional\ndims become `_`, so a write with `tenantId` and a read without it hit **different** keys\n— always pass the same dims you wrote with. There is no dual-read of older layouts; if\nyou previously wrote under a different index shape, reindex or wipe.\n\n## Which `Scope` fields each adapter honors\n\n| Adapter | `threadId` | `userId` | `tenantId` | `namespace` |\n|---------|------------|----------|------------|-------------|\n| `inMemory()` | yes (exact) | yes (exact) | yes (exact) | ignored |\n| `redis()` | yes (key segment) | yes (key segment) | yes (key segment) | ignored |\n| `hindsight()` | yes (bank id) | yes (bank id / `user` option) | yes (bank prefix; unset → `_`) | ignored |\n| `mem0()` | yes (`run_id`) | yes (`user_id` / `user` option) | **no** | ignored |\n| `honcho()` | yes (session key) | yes (peer id / `user` option) | yes (session/peer prefix) | ignored |\n\nOptional dims are exact-match (omit ≠ match any). mem0 does not model tenants —\nencode multi-tenant isolation into `user` if needed.\n\n## `hindsight()`\n\nHosted adapter backed by Hindsight. Owns extraction/ranking server-side and exposes\n`retain`/`recall`/`reflect` LLM tools through `recall`. `@vectorize-io/hindsight-client`\nis an optional peer, loaded lazily.\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Purpose |\n|--------|------|---------|---------|\n| `user` | `string` | `scope.userId` | Durable user id used in the bank key (`{tenant\\|_}__{user}__{threadId}`). |\n| `baseUrl` | `string` | `HINDSIGHT_URL` / `http://localhost:8888` | Server URL. |\n| `budget` | `'low' \\| 'mid' \\| 'high'` | `'mid'` | Recall budget. |\n| `onToolRetain` | `(receipt) => void` | none | Fired when the model calls `hindsight_retain`. |\n| `onToolRecall` | `(query, result) => void` | none | Fired when the model calls `hindsight_recall`. |\n\n```ts\nimport { hindsight } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/hindsight'\n\nconst memory = hindsight({\n  user: 'alice', // bank = {_}__alice__{threadId} (or tenant__alice__{threadId})\n  baseUrl: 'https://hindsight.internal', // default: HINDSIGHT_URL\n  budget: 'high', // deeper recall\n  onToolRetain: (receipt) => console.log('model retained', receipt.ok),\n  onToolRecall: (query, result) =>\n    console.log('model recalled', query, result.fragments?.length),\n})\n```\n\nBank id is `{tenantId|_}__{user}__{threadId}`.\n\n## `mem0()`\n\nHosted adapter backed by a mem0 server, over plain HTTP (no SDK peer). Requires a running\nmem0 server.\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Purpose |\n|--------|------|---------|---------|\n| `user` | `string` | `scope.userId` / `'demo-user'` | mem0 `user_id`. |\n| `baseUrl` | `string` | `MEM0_URL` / `http://localhost:8000` | Server URL. |\n| `apiKey` | `string` | `MEM0_ADMIN_API_KEY` | Bearer token. |\n| `rerank` | `boolean` | `true` | Ask mem0 to rerank search results. |\n| `threshold` | `number` | `0.1` | Minimum search score. |\n\n```ts\nimport { mem0 } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/mem0'\n\nconst memory = mem0({\n  user: 'alice', // mem0 user_id\n  baseUrl: 'https://mem0.internal', // default: MEM0_URL\n  apiKey: process.env.MEM0_ADMIN_API_KEY, // bearer token\n  rerank: true, // rerank results\n  threshold: 0.2, // stricter score floor\n})\n```\n\nmem0 requests send `user_id` and `run_id` (`threadId`). `tenantId` is not sent.\n\n## `honcho()`\n\nHosted adapter backed by Honcho. `recall` returns a synthesized dialectic answer over the\nuser's representation (no discrete fragments). `@honcho-ai/sdk` is an optional peer,\nloaded lazily.\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Purpose |\n|--------|------|---------|---------|\n| `user` | `string` | `scope.userId` / `'demo-user'` | User peer id. |\n| `baseURL` | `string` | `HONCHO_URL` / `http://localhost:8001` | Server URL. |\n| `workspaceId` | `string` | `HONCHO_APP_NAME` / `'ai-memory'` | Workspace id. |\n| `apiKey` | `string` | `HONCHO_API_KEY` / `'dev-no-auth'` | API key. |\n| `assistantId` | `string` | `'assistant'` | Assistant peer id. |\n\n```ts\nimport { honcho } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/honcho'\n\nconst memory = honcho({\n  user: 'alice', // user peer\n  baseURL: 'https://honcho.internal', // default: HONCHO_URL\n  workspaceId: 'my-app', // default: HONCHO_APP_NAME\n  apiKey: process.env.HONCHO_API_KEY, // default: 'dev-no-auth'\n  assistantId: 'support-bot', // default: 'assistant'\n})\n```\n\nHoncho session key is `{tenantId|_}__{threadId}`; peers are `{tenantId}__{user}` when\n`tenantId` is set, otherwise the bare user id.\n\n## Third-party adapters\n\nThese adapters are published and maintained outside TanStack AI. They implement the same\n`recall`/`save` contract, so they drop into `memoryMiddleware` like the ones above.\n\n| Adapter | Package | Backend | Recall |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [`upstashMemory()`](../community-adapters/upstash#memory) | `@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai/memory` | Upstash Redis (HTTP client) | BM25 full-text query in Redis Search |\n\n`upstashMemory()` passes `runMemoryAdapterContract` from `@tanstack/ai-memory/testkit`.\nUnlike `redis()`, it ranks in Redis instead of loading records to rank client-side, and\nit honors `namespace` as well as `tenantId`, `userId`, and `threadId`.\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- [Overview](./overview): the `recall`/`save` contract and how a turn flows\n- [Quickstart](./quickstart): wire an adapter into a real `chat()` call\n- [Operating memory](./operating): options, telemetry, devtools events, and failures\n- [Custom Adapter](./custom-adapter): implement `recall`/`save` for a backend that isn't shipped\n"}
